<!DOCTYPE html>
{#
  VeloMelder report-confirmation e-mail. Sent from ReportSubmissionService::submit() via a
  TemplatedEmail (htmlTemplate + textTemplate, see report_confirmation.txt.twig). Built on the
  canonical bulletproof-table structure documented in VeloWetzikon_Design_Tokens/design-system/
  email.html / email-template.html -- trimmed to only the blocks this specific e-mail needs
  (logo, paragraphs, one primary button, footer -- no secondary button/lists/content image, since
  none of those fit a confirmation e-mail honestly). Keep both in sync if the template's structure
  changes; don't let this drift into its own one-off pattern.

  Logo URL: {{ absolute_url(asset(...)) }}, not a config parameter -- this runs inside the POST
  /reports HTTP request, so the current request's own scheme+host (test-backend vs backend) is
  already correct, exactly like confirmUrl's UrlGeneratorInterface::ABSOLUTE_URL below in
  ReportSubmissionService. No new environment-specific setting needed.
#}
<html lang="de" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:v="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml" xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge">
<meta name="color-scheme" content="light">
<meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light">
<title>Velofreundliches Wetzikon</title>
<!--[if mso]>
<noscript>
<xml>
<o:OfficeDocumentSettings>
<o:PixelsPerInch>96</o:PixelsPerInch>
</o:OfficeDocumentSettings>
</xml>
</noscript>
<style>
  table { border-collapse: collapse; }
  td, a, body { font-family: Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif !important; }
</style>
<![endif]-->
<style>
  body, table, td, a { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; }
  table, td { mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt; }
  img { -ms-interpolation-mode: bicubic; border: 0; height: auto; line-height: 100%; outline: none; text-decoration: none; }
  body { margin: 0; padding: 0; width: 100% !important; background: #fafaf8; }
  a { color: #dc3406; }
  @media screen and (max-width: 600px) {
    .email-container { width: 100% !important; }
    .email-padded { padding-left: 20px !important; padding-right: 20px !important; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body style="margin:0;padding:0;background:#fafaf8;">

{#- UTM-tagged links back to the public site (logo, Impressum) -- utm_content is the only part
    that varies per link, so the shared source/medium/campaign live in one place. Not used in
    report_confirmation.txt.twig: the plain-text part shows the raw URL in full, and a
    query-string-laden link reads as clutter/looks suspicious there in a way it doesn't as a
    hyperlink's invisible href in HTML. If this e-mail's campaign ever needs to differ from
    another e-mail's, change utmCampaign here, not inline at each href. -#}
{%- set utmCampaign = 'meldung_bestaetigung' -%}
{%- set siteUtmBase = 'utm_source=velomelder&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=' ~ utmCampaign -%}

<div style="display:none;max-height:0;overflow:hidden;mso-hide:all;font-size:1px;line-height:1px;color:#fafaf8;">
  {#- Deliberately doesn't repeat "bestätigen" (already in the subject, visible right next to this
      in the inbox list) -- tells the reader something new instead: whose turn it is, and roughly
      where. addressPhrase already picks "bei X" vs "in der Nähe von X" (see
      ReportSubmissionService::addressPhraseForEmail()); reused as-is so both read correctly. -#}
  {{- addressPhrase ? 'Deine Meldung ' ~ addressPhrase ~ ' wartet auf dich.' : 'Deine Meldung wartet auf dich.' -}}
</div>

<center style="width:100%;background:#fafaf8;">
<!--[if mso]>
<table role="presentation" width="600" align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td>
<![endif]-->
<table role="presentation" class="email-container" align="center" width="600" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="margin:0 auto;max-width:600px;width:100%;">

  <tr>
    <td class="email-padded" style="padding:32px 32px 24px;" align="left">
      <a href="https://velofreundliches-wetzikon.ch/?{{ siteUtmBase }}&amp;utm_content=logo" target="_blank">
        <img src="{{ absolute_url(asset('assets/email/logo.png')) }}" width="168" height="29" alt="Velofreundliches Wetzikon" style="display:block;border:0;outline:none;text-decoration:none;max-width:168px;" />
      </a>
    </td>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e8e6e0;border-radius:8px;">
      <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
        <tr>
          <td class="email-padded" style="padding:40px 40px 32px;">

            {# name/addressPhrase/ratingLabel: see ReportSubmissionService::submit() -- all three
               are null-safe (anonymous report, un-geocodable location, or a missing rating row
               that can't actually happen given the 1-5 validation, but the template doesn't
               assume it). addressPhrase is a ready-to-embed phrase ("bei X"/"in der Nähe von X"),
               not a bare address -- the two cases need different connecting words.

               Built via {% set %} + a single {{ }} print, not inline {% if %} block tags --
               Twig silently eats the newline immediately after every block tag by default, which
               makes exact whitespace (blank lines in report_confirmation.txt.twig) fragile to get
               right with inline if/else. A {{ }} print tag has no such behavior. #}
            {%- set ratingSuffix = ratingLabel ? ' (Bewertung: ' ~ ratingLabel ~ ')' : '' -%}
            {%- set thanksSentence = addressPhrase
                ? 'vielen Dank für deine Meldung zur Stelle ' ~ addressPhrase ~ ratingSuffix ~ '.'
                : 'vielen Dank für deine Meldung zu einer von dir gemeldeten Stelle' ~ ratingSuffix ~ '.'
            -%}
            <p style="margin:0 0 16px;font-family:Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:#000000;">
              Hallo{% if name %} {{ name }}{% endif %},<br><br>
              {{ thanksSentence }}
            </p>
            <p style="margin:0 0 24px;font-family:Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:#000000;">
              Bitte bestätige deine Meldung über den Button unten &ndash; anschliessend wird sie geprüft und veröffentlicht.
            </p>

            <!-- Primary button -- bulletproof VML+HTML pattern, see email.html#buttons for the
                 arcsize math (4px radius at 44px height -> 18%). -->
            <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="margin:0 0 24px;">
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <!--[if mso]>
                  <v:roundrect xmlns:v="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" href="{{ confirmUrl }}" style="height:44px;v-text-anchor:middle;width:220px;" arcsize="18%" stroke="f" fillcolor="#dc3406">
                  <w:anchorlock/>
                  <center style="color:#ffffff;font-family:Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.01em;">Meldung bestätigen</center>
                  </v:roundrect>
                  <![endif]-->
                  <!--[if !mso]><!-->
                  <a href="{{ confirmUrl }}" target="_blank" style="background-color:#dc3406;border-radius:4px;color:#ffffff;display:inline-block;font-family:Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.01em;line-height:44px;text-align:center;text-decoration:none;width:220px;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;mso-hide:all;">Meldung bestätigen</a>
                  <!--<![endif]-->
                </td>
              </tr>
            </table>

            <p style="margin:0 0 24px;font-family:Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6;color:#5e5e5a;">
              Der Link ist {{ ttlHours }} Stunden gültig. Falls du diese Meldung nicht abgeschickt hast, kannst du diese E-Mail einfach ignorieren &ndash; ohne Bestätigung wird nichts veröffentlicht.
            </p>

            <p style="margin:0 0 16px;font-family:Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:#000000;">
              Danke, dass du Wetzikon velofreundlicher machst.
            </p>

            <p style="margin:0;font-family:Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:#000000;">
              Dein Team von<br>Velofreundliches Wetzikon
            </p>

          </td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </td>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td class="email-padded" style="padding:24px 32px 40px;text-align:center;font-family:Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:1.6;color:#8a8a86;">
      Velofreundliches Wetzikon &mdash; private Initiative<br>
      Thom Hoffmann &middot; Messikommerstrasse 37 &middot; 8620 Wetzikon<br>
      <a href="https://velofreundliches-wetzikon.ch/impressum-editor/?{{ siteUtmBase }}&amp;utm_content=impressum" style="color:#8a8a86;text-decoration:underline;">Impressum</a>
    </td>
  </tr>

</table>
<!--[if mso]></td></tr></table><![endif]-->
</center>
</body>
</html>
